# Sangbik .dockerignore — what must NEVER go into the Docker build context.
# This file controls the build context only; it does NOT control runtime
# caches. Model caches (~/.cache/huggingface, Whisper ~464 MB, NLLB) are
# downloaded at runtime on first workflow use (lazy) and are never committed.
# NEVER commit / upload these, especially to a PUBLIC Space:
#   - any .env file (keys belong only in the host's secret settings, never in code)
#   - sangbik-release.keystore / any *.keystore (the Android signing key)
#   - server/.venv, node_modules, client/dist (rebuilt in the image)
#   - server/uploads, server/outputs, server/data (user videos/results/projects;
#     on free hosts these are ephemeral anyway — download results before restart)
.git
.github
.env
.env.*
*.keystore
sangbik-release.keystore
**/node_modules
server/.venv
server/node_modules
client/node_modules
client/dist
server/uploads
server/outputs
server/data
**/.cache
**/models--*
*.log
.DS_Store
